{"type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn11le08ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le08ob03re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn11le08ob03re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn11le08ob03re2img01.jpg", "text": "Sari's boyfriend, Tony, was a photographer who often traveled to exotic locations for work. Sari detested Tony's constant traveling. She objected to his disappearing for days at a time with little to no contact, but she put up with it out of devotion. Every week she would wait eagerly for his phone call, but he didn't always catch her at home. Sari's roommate, Louise, got used to taking very detailed messages. Louise disliked their putting her in the middle of the relationship, but she conscientiously recorded the messages regardless.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn11le08ob03re2img02.jpg", "text": "One time, Sari came home from work and saw that Tony had called. She resented his having left another message, but of course she was pleased to receive an update.<br/>\"Louise, when did Tony call?\" Sari asked.<br/>\n\"He called at about 4:30. He said he would call back later,\" Louise replied.<br/>\n\"Did he give you an update?\" Sari asked.<br/>\n\"He said that he may have lost his passport in the Amazon jungle, and that he would have to go back to the field site to locate it. He mentioned that one of the more enterprising assistants might have found it and stored it for him. However he did add that it may have been lost for good, in which case he would have to stay a few extra weeks in the region,\" Louise said.<br/>\n\"Did he say how he was?\" Sari asked.<br/>\n\"Yes. He said that he was fine despite the complications, and that the rainforest was really stunning. He said that he might have even taken some award-caliber pictures,\" Louise answered.", "time": "38900", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn11le08ob03re2img03.jpg", "text": "\"Did he say when he was coming back?\" Sari asked.<br/>\n\"He said that he might have been able to catch a flight in early August, but because of the delay, it might be more like September,\" Louise said.<br/>About an hour later, Tony himself called. This time, Sari answered. <br/>\n\"Sari, I have so much to tell you!\" he said.<br/>\n\"Oh, I heard it all from Louise already,\" she answered. \"Everything is the same here. Um, I guess I'll speak to you next week. Bye!\"", "time": "103000", "id": 3}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about people's personalities, love and marriage.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express uncertainty about past events.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about two actions together.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " When you are traveling, how do you communicate with your friends and family?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do you prefer to talk, text or e-mail? Explain your choice.", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": " Let's find out how the long-distance relationship is working out!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "STI", "questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "